   "about": "A guide to Japan’s wartime production controls and proposed Military Government administration of essential production after occupation.",
   "summary": "The guide surveys national, regional, and local economic controls, including ministries, Control Societies, Munitions Companies, National Policy Companies, and Eidan. It proposes priorities, allocations, and credit to support occupation forces, minimum civilian needs, exports, and repair of essential facilities. It recommends retaining useful controls initially while abolishing the Munitions Ministry and coercive industry associations, and giving smaller enterprises a stronger role. This section ends during its recommendations for regional and local control; the guide continues beyond page 40.",
